{"ts": "2026-11-01T22:29:49.125Z", "task": "T-2026-11-01-2224-dump-ai-reports-task", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-created-falls-back-to-int-0-against-stri-3c5e: created() falls back to int 0 against string ts in the characterization harness", "data": {"rkey": "R-created-falls-back-to-int-0-against-stri-3c5e", "title": "created() falls back to int 0 against string ts in the characterization harness", "where": ["tests/test_state_characterization.py:253"], "label": "RISK", "what": "Scratch.created() returns 0 when events.jsonl is missing or unparseable, but real journals carry ISO-string ts; a report dir without a journal next to ones with one makes task_ids() (now also called by files_dump) raise TypeError comparing int and str. No current scenario hits it. Fix: return '' as the fallback and test the missing-journal path. (T-2026-11-01-2224 review L1)", "likelihood": null, "fix": null, "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-01T22:29:55.895Z", "task": "T-2026-11-01-2224-dump-ai-reports-task", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-full-golden-flakes-when-its-two-tasks-st-34db: full golden flakes when its two tasks start in different minutes", "data": {"rkey": "R-full-golden-flakes-when-its-two-tasks-st-34db", "title": "full golden flakes when its two tasks start in different minutes", "where": ["tests/test_state_characterization.py:266"], "label": "RISK", "what": "files_dump walks .ai/reports/ in path order; task ids are T-<date>-<HHMM>-<slug>, so the golden (both tasks in one minute) dumps <ID2> 'drop-the-table' before <ID1>; a run that crosses a minute boundary (likely under the parallel suite, test_full took 16.6s) dumps them the other way and test_full fails with a 725-line diff. Seen in T-2026-11-01-2141 suite run 5.", "likelihood": "on a loaded machine or CI, about once per many runs", "fix": "dump .ai/reports/<id>/ in the order of task_ids() (creation order), not path order", "status": "fixed", "status_why": "files_dump orders .ai/reports/<id>/ and .ai/state/logs/<id>/ by task_ids() (creation order); test_dump_orders_tasks_by_creation pins both parents, same-minute and cross-minute; full.txt regenerated (swap only)", "supersedes": "r1-94adea24983ff494a2a985cc"}}
